Skip GDAL's target-Python probe when the Python bindings are switched off.

flet-libgdal builds the libgdal C/C++ library only: build.sh passes
-DBUILD_PYTHON_BINDINGS=OFF on both the Android and the iOS leg, and the Python
bindings live in their own recipe (recipes/gdal). GDAL 3.13 nevertheless runs
its `find_package(Python ... COMPONENTS Interpreter Development NumPy)` block
unconditionally near the top of CMakeLists.txt, long before anything consults
BUILD_PYTHON_BINDINGS.

Searching for the Interpreter/Development components while cross-compiling is
precisely what CMake 4.x's policy CMP0190 refuses to do unless an emulator has
been declared -- "Interpreter and/or Compiler components cannot be searched
when CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR variable is not specified" -- so configure
aborts on every slice, over a Python we never wanted found.

The patch wraps the block in

    if (BUILD_PYTHON_BINDINGS OR NOT DEFINED BUILD_PYTHON_BINDINGS)

Our build.sh passes OFF, so the probe is skipped; anyone configuring GDAL
without mentioning the option at all still gets upstream's behaviour. Without
this hunk flet-libgdal 3.13.x does not configure at all.

Added with the flet-libgdal 3.10.0 -> 3.13.1 bump (PR #68, which describes it
as guarding "GDAL 3.13's new unconditional find_package(Python) block behind
BUILD_PYTHON_BINDINGS so it doesn't trip CMake 4.x's CMP0190 cross-compile
policy"). The other 3.13 regression that PR dealt with -- FindOpenMP picking up
the build host's libgomp and stamping a DT_NEEDED on libomp.so that Android's
Python runtime cannot satisfy -- is handled by -DGDAL_USE_OPENMP=OFF in
build.sh, not here.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -221,6 +221,12 @@ endif()
 endif()
 set(ENV{MKL_ENABLE_INSTRUCTIONS} "SSE4_2")

+# Mobile cross-compile guard: GDAL 3.13 unconditionally probes for the
+# target Python interpreter even when -DBUILD_PYTHON_BINDINGS=OFF. Under
+# CMake 4.x that trips policy CMP0190 ("Interpreter and/or Compiler
+# components cannot be searched when CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR
+# variable is not specified"). Skip the block when bindings are off.
+if (BUILD_PYTHON_BINDINGS OR NOT DEFINED BUILD_PYTHON_BINDINGS)
 if (Python_LOOKUP_VERSION)
     set(Python_FIND_STRATEGY VERSION)
     find_package(Python ${Python_LOOKUP_VERSION} EXACT COMPONENTS Interpreter Development NumPy)
@@ -248,6 +254,7 @@ if (Python_Interpreter_FOUND)
     endif ()
   endif()
 endif()
+endif()

 # Restore previous value of MKL_ENABLE_INSTRUCTIONS
 if(DEFINED BACKUP_ENV_VAR_MKL_ENABLE_INSTRUCTIONS)
